<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Baardheere</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Bardera</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Baardheere, also written Bardera, is a town on the Jubba river in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/somalia">Somalia</a>. In 1819 a community of militant religious reformers founded a settlement there that tried to impose strict Islamic practice on the surrounding region and fought neighbouring powers. In 1843 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultan">Sultan</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yusuf-mahamud-ibrahim">Yusuf Mahamud Ibrahim</a> of the Geledi led a large coalition that destroyed the Bardera community.</p></div>
